invariant: INV-24
file: x25519.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh x25519_step
reason: turning the step's last square into an add of e to itself hands
  the next step a b whose limbs reach 2^18, twice the bound the field-op
  proofs assume. bin/unit fails on it too, since b is then 2e rather
  than e squared; the violation checks that the proof sees the bound on
  its own, which is what a rewrite that keeps the vectors right and the
  limbs wide would need (https://github.com/c4milo/chapulin/pull/117
  measured 2 of x25519_step's 473 properties failing). Each run is a
  proof of minutes, so this belongs to the nightly's
  test-invariants-proof-backed job, never the fast tier.

--- old
    sqr(b, e);
    cswap(a, b, r);
--- new
    add(b, e, e);
    cswap(a, b, r);
